-- title:
--   Smoothness of relative dimension one of the projective Weierstrass model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $V$ be a Weierstrass cubic over $R$ in the projective sense, i.e. a datum of coefficients $a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,a_6\in R$ presented as a homogeneous cubic in three variables, and assume $V$ is elliptic in Mathlib's sense, namely that its discriminant is a unit of $R$. Consider the graded ring obtained by taking the homogeneous components of the polynomial ring in the three variables indexed by `Fin 3` over $R$ and passing to the quotient by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $V$; this grading is `projModelGradingCR V`, a family of $R$-submodules of the quotient ring indexed by $\mathbb{N}$. Let $\mathrm{Proj}$ of that grading be equipped with the structure morphism `projModelStrCR V` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$, defined as the canonical morphism $\mathrm{Proj} \to \operatorname{Spec}$ of the degree-zero part followed by the morphism of spectra induced by the structure map $R \to (\text{degree-}0\text{ part})$. The assertion is that this morphism is smooth of relative dimension $1$ in the sense of Mathlib's `SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1`: locally on source and target it is given by a standard smooth ring map of relative dimension one.
--
--   This is the statement that the projective plane model of a Weierstrass cubic with invertible discriminant is a smooth relative curve over the base ring, the geometric input behind treating an elliptic curve over a ring as a smooth proper relative curve of dimension one. It is invoked throughout the project wherever the Weierstrass model must be used as a scheme smooth over its base, for instance in the construction of relative group laws and quaternionic moduli in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassProjModel_projModelStrCR_smoothOfRelativeDimension_one.lean

